        "original_id": "8cb49bcc-c714-5b0d-83f4-9c6a985f03b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Trade unions in the United Kingdom, Labour Representation Committee, Labour Party\n- People: Tony Blair\n- Places: United Kingdom, Britain\n- Topics: Trade union movement, British politics\n\nFacts:\n- Trade unions in the United Kingdom were legalised in 1871.\n- The trade union movement in Britain sought to reform socio-economic conditions for working men in British industries.\n- The trade unions' search for reform led to the creation of the Labour Representation Committee.\n- The Labour Representation Committee effectively formed the basis for today's Labour Party.\n- The Labour Party still has extensive links with the trade union movement in Britain.\n- Tony Blair was born on 6 May 1953.\n- Tony Blair served as Leader of the Labour Party from 21 July 1994 to 24 June 2007.\n- Tony Blair served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 2 May 1997 to 27 June 2007.",
